### 1. Standard vs. Itemized Deduction
**You should take the Standard Deduction.**
For 2024, the standard deduction for Married Filing Jointly is **$29,200**. 
To itemize, your deductible expenses (state/local taxes capped at $10,000, mortgage interest, and charity) would need to exceed $29,200. Your known itemizable expenses are your $720 charitable donation and your Oregon state taxes (roughly $6,000–$8,000). Because this is far below $29,200, the standard deduction is much more beneficial for you. 
